          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            Where a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %em parameterization
            of such a model is a sigma-model (subject usually to some constraints) whose target space now is the total space of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            when restricted to fields that take values only in any one
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
          %p
            Parameterized WZW models have been argued to provide a more geometric and more complete description of the
            = succeed "-sector" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebra"} current algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            backgrounds than the traditional construction in terms of worldsheet fermions (
            %a{:href => "#GatesSiegel88"}> Gates-Siegel 88
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GKKS91"} Gates-Ketov-Kozenko-Solovev 91
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe10"} Distler-Sharpe 10, section 7
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly"} Green-Schwarz anomaly
            of the heterotic string finds a natural interpretation as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            to parameterizing the given WZW term over the given principal bundle:
          %p
            A (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"}> higher
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            is an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and whose
            = succeed "-part" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{WZW}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  G \longrightarrow
                  \\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
          %p
            (whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            is given by the global
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
            on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            If one has a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  G &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; B
                  }
          %p
            over some base space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift+of+the+structure+group"} lift of the structure group
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+n-group"} Heisenberg n-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Heis
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heis_G(\mathbf{L}_{WZW})
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{WZW}
            regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundle"} prequantum n-bundle
            = succeed "-wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{WZW}
            glue fiberwise to a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                    %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{WZW}^X \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
          %p
            on the total space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of this bundle. This hence yields what one may think of as a coherent collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+models"} WZW models
            %em parameterized
            over base space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            For the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+group"} semisimple Lie group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{WZW}
            its canonical WZW term (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} 2-connection
            on the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Heis
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi WZW
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi String
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Heis_G(\mathbf{L}_{WZW})\simeq String(G)
          %p
            and hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            to the existence of a parameterization is precisely a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly"} Green-Schwarz anomaly
            (see
            %a{:href => "#cwzw"} cwzw
            for details of this claim).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#the_heterotic_string The heterotic string
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            combined with a chiral
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = Spin \times E_8 \times E_8
            or similar and with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"} WZW term
            being the difference between the differentially twisted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping"} looping
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} universal Chern-Simons 3-connection
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin
            with that of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 8
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8 \times E_8
          %p
            By (
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaRogersSchreiber13"}> Fiorenza-Rogers-Schreiber 13, section 2.6.1
            ) we find in this case that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+2-group"} Heisenberg 2-group
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Heis
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi WZW
                        %mi het
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi String
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Heis(\mathbf{L}_{WZW^{het}})
                  \\simeq
                  String(G)
                  \\,.
          %p
            It follows thus from the above discussion that a consistent heterotic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
            requires that the underlying
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            admits a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly"} Green-Schwarz anomaly
            cancellation condition, re-expressed as a consistency condition for parameterized WZW models.
          %p
            On the level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"} action functionals
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            0 this observation is due to (
            %a{:href => "#DistlerSharpe10"}> Distler-Sharpe 10, section 7
            ).
          %h3#the_greenschwarz_super_branes_on_curved_super_spacetime
            The Green-Schwarz super
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            By
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber13"} Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 13
            the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ;
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1;N}
            classified by the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} the brane bouqet
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi WZW
                        %mi brane
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ;
                      %mi N
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{WZW^{brane}}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1;N} \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}^{p+1}(\mathbb{R}/\Gamma)_{conn}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is the group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periods"} periods
            of the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ cocycle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi sIso
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B} sIso_N(d-1,1) \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}^{p+2}(\mathbb{R}/\Gamma)
                  \\,.
          %p
            A necessary structure globalizing this to a curved super-spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi QuantMorph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi WZW
                        %mi brane
                    %mi inf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = \mathbf{QuantMorph}(\mathbf{L}_{WZW^{brane}}^{inf})
            the restriction of the WZW term to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk"} infinitesimal disk
          %p
            Given this then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            refines to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            datum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi WZW
                        %mi brane
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}_{WZW^{brane}}
            globally defined on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            (For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            on which other branes may end, such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            is replaced by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+Minkowski+super+spacetime"} extended Minkowski super spacetime
            = succeed "))." do
              %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber13"} Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 13
          %p
            More details are in (
            %a{:href => "#cwzw"}> cwzw
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+WZW+model"} gauged WZW model
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalization+of+WZW+term"} definite globalization of WZW term
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher Cartan geometry
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Parameterized WZW models as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+models"} sigma models
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            originate in
          %ul
            %li#GatesSiegel88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Warren+Siegel"} Warren Siegel
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Leftons, Rightons, Nonlinear
                    = succeed "-Models," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/record/251286/"} spire
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strings, superstrings, and two-dimensional lagrangian field theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Functional integration, geometry, and strings
            %li#GKKS91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
                , S. Ketov, S. Kozenko, O. Solovev,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Lagrangian chiral coset construction of heterotic string theories in
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,0)
                    superspace
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/314337/?ln=en"} spire
          %p
            Discussion relating this to equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genera"} elliptic genera
            is in section 7 of
          %ul
            %li#DistlerSharpe10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"}> Jacques Distler
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"} Eric Sharpe
              = succeed "," do
                %em Heterotic compactifications with principal bundles for general groups and general levels
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0701244"} arXiv:hep-th/0701244
          %p Review of this includes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"}> Eric Sharpe
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Recent developments in heterotic compactifications
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Sharpe"} Eric Sharpe
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+Greenspoon"} Arthur Greenspoon
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=AMSIP-44"} Advances in String Theory: The First Sowers Workshop in Theoretical Physics
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.phys.vt.edu/sowers/talks/sharpe-sowers.pdf"} pdf slides (39-49)
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genera"} elliptic genera
            had been considered in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The sigma orientation for analytic circle-equivariant elliptic cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0201092"} arXiv:math/0201092
          %p
            and with more emphasis on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant elliptic cohomology and the Fibered WZW models of Distler and Sharpe
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ucsb.edu/~drm/GTPseminar/2007-fall.php"} talk 2007
              (
              %a{:href => "https://web.archive.org/web/20150326114418/https://www.math.ucsb.edu/~drm/GTPseminar/notes/20071026-ando/20071026-malmendier.pdf"}> lecture notes pdf
              )
          %p
            The discussion of the relevant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+n-group"} Heisenberg n-group
            theory is in
          %ul
            %li#FiorenzaRogersSchreiber13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+geometric+prequantum+theory"} Higher geometric prequantum theory
